  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem. Nothing in the archive describes Command Palette blocking the \\\"|\\\" character in non-elevated apps while it works in elevated ones. The closest tickets were about other problems. PowerToys#42204 turned out to be a \\\"+\\\" alias for an extension that wasn't running. PowerToys#41736 is about aliases eating keystrokes when you type fast. PowerToys#38297 is about hotkey handling. None of them match. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. Add the PowerToys bug report ZIP and your keyboard layout. Also say whether any Command Palette alias or global hotkey is set to \\\"|\\\" or to a key combination that produces it, such as Shift+\\\\. Say whether the problem still happens with the Command Palette hotkey and aliases cleared. As a temporary workaround, turn Command Palette off while you need to type \\\"|\\\".\"}",
